Z||000007||rprevo||04-09-2001||06:42 PM|||| I put the Meziere 35 GPM electric water<BR>pump in mine and it has a 2000 hr. warranty<BR>the people at Meziere are great and the<BR>pump was 300 bucks The Morrosso was only<BR>19 GPM and with it being 90 degrees outside<BR>I was running 70 mph with the 4:10 gear<BR>I would run about 220 to 225 with this<BR>Meziere I Havn't seen over 165 in 70 degree<BR>wheather so far. As far as coolant Passing<BR>to fast if your thermostat is working properly you have a degree of restriction<BR>untill it opens cause your coolant should go <BR>through your Heater core and Back to the<BR>Radiator then the thermostat opens and the<BR>abundence of heat comes from the big water<BR>neck. I put my water pump in place of the spare tire and made a Manifold to feed<BR>the engine block. I can E-Mail pictures<BR>but I don't know how to put them on this site<P>350 chevy 360 hp<P>     Ray<BR>||||reg||1
